  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1419:86 steps total. Phases 0–9 are the delivered Workflow 
Builder foundation (51 steps, complete).
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1420:Phases 10–16 are the provider-platform migration and 
become the next work — 31 steps:
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1421:audit/contracts (10), shared runtime (11), generic UI 
and nodes (12), domain migrations (13–15),
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1422:then SDK/cleanup/final compatibility gate (16). The 
platform covers **five** domains: `script`,
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1423:`scene_blueprint`, `tts`, `storyboard`, `animator`. 
Music and Captions are deliberately excluded
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1424:(owner decision, 2026-08-08) because they are local 
single-implementation services with no provider
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1425:dimension; they keep their existing nodes and code, 
and the plan's job is to prove they still work.
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1426:Distribution moves to Phase 17 so releases and the 
Workflow Copilot build on the stable plugin
> _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1427:platform. The provider critical path is **10.1 → 10.2 
→ 10.3 → 10.4 → 11.1 → 11.3 → 11.4 →
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1428:11.5 → 12.1 → 12.2 → 12.3 → 12.5**, after which 
domain migrations can proceed in parallel before
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1429:16.1–16.5. Treat **11.4** (result/error boundary), 
**12.3** (saved node migration), and **14.1**
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1430:(async job reconciliation) with the most care: 
mistakes there can silently corrupt artifacts,
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1431:invalidate caches, or report failed provider work as 
successful.
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1432:
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1433:Three risks are specific to this codebase and are 
easy to underestimate:
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1434:
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1435:- **The existing provider interfaces have never 
run.** Phases 11/14/15 are first-time wiring, not a
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1436:  refactor of working code. Budget for the seven 
`provider.py` bodies being stale or wrong, and capture
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1437:  legacy-path fixtures *before* rewiring so there is 
something real to diff against.
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1438:- **12.2 gates 15.2.** Provider-dependent dropdowns 
are impossible until
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1439:  `GET /api/workflow/options/<source>` accepts 
context. If 12.2 ships without it, 15.2 cannot deliver
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1440:  per-provider voices and will either stall or 
smuggle a provider ID back into the UI.
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1441:- **12.3 converts two nodes whose domains have no 
providers yet.** The `builtin` passthrough rule in
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1442:  that step is what keeps the app working between 
Phase 12 and Phase 13; dropping it strands
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1443:  Script and Scene Blueprint on an empty catalog.
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1444:- **Music and Captions are out of scope and must stay 
that way.** Their `mode`/`tone`/`preset` fields
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1445:  look like provider selection but are not. An agent 
doing a thorough job on 12.3 or 16.1 will be
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1446:  tempted to "finish" them; every step that touches 
those two nodes must instead prove they are
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:1447:  byte-identical.
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\contracts.md:19:| D1 | `studio/scenes` module | Does not exist. Scene generation 
is `studio/build_scene_blueprints/` (blueprint name `scenes`, routes `/api/scenes/*`) | Adapters import from 
`studio.build_scene_blueprints.*` |
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\contracts.md:20:| D2 | `studio/assets` module | Does not exist. The "assets" step 
is `studio/animator/` (`animation_routes.py` grabber + `organizer.py`) | Animator node wraps `studio.animator`; 
"assets" is UI vocabulary only |
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\contracts.md:21:| D3 | Assemble consumes audio+scenes+assets via data edges | 
`_step_assemble(project_id)` takes **only** `project_id` and reads everything from disk (`routes.py:1919`) | Assemble 
node keeps typed input ports for **ordering/readiness**, but the adapter contract is: inputs assert artifact presence; 
payload = `project_id` |
> _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\contracts.md:22:| D4 | Storyboard and/or Animator feed Assemble | **Mutually 
exclusive.** `_pick_scene_asset` (`editor/routes.py:72`) reads ONLY `output/animator/`. Storyboard images are 
reference inputs to the animator (base64 side channel, `animation_routes.py:243-256`); no code path puts them on the 
timeline | Assemble's asset input port type is `animation_assets` only. Storyboard output port connects to Animator 
(reference) or Workflow Output — never Assemble. Storyboard→timeline is a possible future adapter feature, out of 
scope v1 |
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\contracts.md:23:| D5 | Resume can reload any step | `_load_prior_results` has 
**no `assets` branch** (`routes.py:793`) — assets are never reloadable in the legacy pipeline | Workflow engine's own 
`run_data` + fingerprint cache supersedes `_load_prior_results`; adapters must not depend on it |
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\contracts.md:24:| D6 | — | `storyboard_provider`, `image_model`, `arguments` are 
declared in `PipelineRunRequest` but never copied into the job config (`routes.py:283-318`) — silently dead in the 
legacy pipeline | Workflow node configs bypass the legacy config dict entirely; adapters receive node configuration 
directly |
> _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\contracts.md:25:| D7 | Project identity can be inferred from every edge payload | 
Legacy artifacts sometimes use a `source_folder` different from the editor `project_id`; several steps reconstruct 
paths from one or the other | Every execution has one immutable project context. New runs allocate `pm_XXXXXX`; 
`project.existing` selects an existing ID before side-effecting nodes start. Artifact outputs carry safe relative refs 
plus `project_id` and `source_folder` where relevant. Adapters consume those fields instead of guessing paths. 
Conflicting existing-project inputs or request/project-node mismatches fail validation. |
